~ sky_meeting
Mother: …
Mother: You’re drifting again.
Mother: Just like you used to.

Player: Am I dreaming?

Mother: Does it matter?
Mother: You always came to me like this.
Mother: When the ground felt too heavy.

Mother: Look down.
Mother: See how small everything is from here.

Player: I tried to stay.
Player: I really did. 

Mother: I know.
Mother: That’s why you’re still standing.

Player: Why now?
Player: Why here?

Mother: Because this is where you listen.
Mother: And because I can only meet you when you stop running.

Mother: You don’t need to hold the weight alone anymore.

- Reach for her
	Mother: …
	Mother: You were never alone.
	Mother: Even when you thought you were.
- Stay silent
	Mother: It’s alright.
	Mother: Silence was always your answer.

Mother: When you wake up—
Mother: you’ll forget the sky.
Mother: But not how it felt.

Mother: That feeling will guide you.
Mother: Let it.

do GameState.mother1_end.emit()

=> END
